# ─── Quality Framework — .env.example ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Header-only seed. Concrete variables are added by the `env-config-awareness`
# skill during Phase 3, one variable per runtime config read — never
# speculatively.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` on your local machine, fill in non-secret values,
# and reference secrets via the vault declared by
# `tech-stack-integrations/secrets-vault.yaml`. The `.env` file itself is
# gitignored — see `.gitignore § Secrets`.
#
# ─── Rules (enforced by `env-config-awareness`) ─────────────────────────────
#
#   1. Every runtime configuration value MUST appear here first, with:
#         # purpose: <one-line description of what the value controls>
#         NAME=<default or the literal token REQUIRED>
#
#   2. Every SECRET value MUST use a vault reference, never a literal:
#         # purpose: token used to authenticate against the payments API
#         PAYMENTS_API_TOKEN=VAULT:<secrets-vault.yaml § naming.path_pattern>
#
#      The literal token `VAULT:` signals to `env-config-awareness` that the
#      real value is fetched at runtime via
#      `secrets-vault.yaml § commands.fetch_runtime`.
#
#   3. `REQUIRED` marks a variable that MUST be supplied by the operator at
#      deploy time. The code path that reads it MUST fail fast on missing.
#
#   4. Never delete a variable from this file without also removing its reader
#      from `src/`. `code-review-gate` will flag orphan config reads.
#
# ─── Ownership ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   - This file is the shared, committed contract.
#   - `.env` (uncommitted) holds the local values.
#   - `secrets-vault.yaml` holds where real secret VALUES live.
#
# See `AGENTS.md § "Ownership boundaries"` and
# `skills/env-config-awareness/SKILL.md`.
#
# ─── Variables ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# (Empty on purpose. Entries are appended per-feature by `env-config-awareness`.)
# purpose: filesystem path of the JSON file holding every persisted Task
TASKMASTER_STORE_PATH=taskmaster.json

